{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5309a753",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ML Zoomcamp HW3\n",
    "\n",
    "**2026 — Classification**\n",
    "\n",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b7c54d4e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup and dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "The target is `converted`. Missing categorical values become `NA`; missing numerical values become `0.0`. If the remote CSV cannot be reached, download it using [this link](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DataTalksClub/machine-learning-zoomcamp/main/cohorts/2026/data/course_lead_scoring_2026.csv) and put it next to this notebook."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "22049ec8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Uncomment if dependencies need installing:\n",
    "# %pip install pandas numpy scikit-learn\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from IPython.display import display\n",
    "from sklearn.feature_extraction import DictVectorizer\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, mutual_info_score\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_URL = (\n",
    "    \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DataTalksClub/machine-learning-zoomcamp/\"\n",
    "    \"main/cohorts/2026/data/course_lead_scoring_2026.csv\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    df = pd.read_csv(DATA_URL)\n",
    "except Exception as exc:\n",
    "    print(f\"Online dataset unavailable ({exc}). Trying local CSV...\")\n",
    "    df = pd.read_csv(\"course_lead_scoring_2026.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Shape:\", df.shape)\n",
    "display(df.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "81d164d9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "target = \"converted\"\n",
    "cat_cols = df.select_dtypes(include=[\"object\", \"category\"]).columns.tolist()\n",
    "num_cols = [col for col in df.select_dtypes(include=\"number\").columns if col != target]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Missing values before filling:\")\n",
    "display(df.isna().sum().to_frame(\"missing\"))\n",
    "df[cat_cols] = df[cat_cols].fillna(\"NA\")\n",
    "df[num_cols] = df[num_cols].fillna(0.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "assert df.isna().sum().sum() == 0, \"Unexpected missing values remain\"\n",
    "print(\"Categorical columns:\", cat_cols)\n",
    "print(\"Numerical columns:\", num_cols)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8ef6672d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q1 — Most common industry\n",
    "\n",
    "Find the mode after categorical missing values are filled."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "95479b55",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "industry_counts = df[\"industry\"].value_counts()\n",
    "display(industry_counts)\n",
    "q1 = industry_counts.idxmax()\n",
    "print(\"Q1 answer:\", q1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c61001d0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q2 — Largest numerical correlation\n",
    "\n",
    "Compare the absolute correlations of **only the four pairs listed in the assignment**; the target is excluded."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a5bafc7f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "correlation = df[num_cols].corr()\n",
    "display(correlation.round(3))\n",
    "\n",
    "candidate_pairs = [\n",
    "    (\"interaction_count\", \"lead_score\"),\n",
    "    (\"number_of_courses_viewed\", \"lead_score\"),\n",
    "    (\"number_of_courses_viewed\", \"interaction_count\"),\n",
    "    (\"annual_income\", \"interaction_count\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "pair_scores = pd.Series({\n",
    "    f\"{left} and {right}\": abs(correlation.loc[left, right])\n",
    "    for left, right in candidate_pairs\n",
    "}).sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "display(pair_scores.to_frame(\"absolute correlation\"))\n",
    "q2 = pair_scores.idxmax()\n",
    "print(\"Q2 answer:\", q2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dc67c346",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Split the dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the exact split parameters specified in the homework. Predictors do not include `converted`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6153c374",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_full_train, df_test = train_test_split(df, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
    "df_train, df_val = train_test_split(\n",
    "    df_full_train, test_size=0.25, random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "y_train = df_train[target].to_numpy()\n",
    "y_val = df_val[target].to_numpy()\n",
    "y_test = df_test[target].to_numpy()\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train = df_train.drop(columns=[target]).copy()\n",
    "X_val = df_val.drop(columns=[target]).copy()\n",
    "X_test = df_test.drop(columns=[target]).copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Training: {len(X_train)} | Validation: {len(X_val)} | Test: {len(X_test)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b66d25c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q3 — Mutual information\n",
    "\n",
    "For categorical predictors, compute mutual information with the target using **training data only**. Round each score to two decimals."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fc19782c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "mi_scores = pd.Series({\n",
    "    feature: round(mutual_info_score(df_train[feature], df_train[target]), 2)\n",
    "    for feature in cat_cols\n",
    "}).sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "display(mi_scores.to_frame(\"mutual information (rounded)\"))\n",
    "q3 = mi_scores.loc[[\"industry\", \"location\", \"lead_source\", \"employment_status\"]].idxmax()\n",
    "print(\"Q3 answer:\", q3)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5bf65843",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q4 — Logistic regression\n",
    "\n",
    "One-hot encode categorical features with `DictVectorizer` and include numerical features. Follow the exact classifier configuration given in the assignment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5d856b16",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def fit_and_score(train_frame, val_frame, train_y=y_train, val_y=y_val, C=1.0):\n",
    "    encoder = DictVectorizer(sparse=True)\n",
    "    train_matrix = encoder.fit_transform(train_frame.to_dict(orient=\"records\"))\n",
    "    val_matrix = encoder.transform(val_frame.to_dict(orient=\"records\"))\n",
    "    classifier = LogisticRegression(\n",
    "        solver=\"liblinear\", C=C, max_iter=1000, random_state=42\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    classifier.fit(train_matrix, train_y)\n",
    "    predictions = classifier.predict(val_matrix)\n",
    "    return accuracy_score(val_y, predictions), classifier, encoder\n",
    "\n",
    "base_accuracy, model, dv = fit_and_score(X_train, X_val)\n",
    "q4 = round(base_accuracy, 2)\n",
    "print(f\"Validation accuracy: {base_accuracy:.6f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Q4 answer (2 decimals): {q4:.2f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7c792dc3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q5 — Feature elimination\n",
    "\n",
    "Remove one of the three nominated **original columns** at a time, then retrain the full pipeline. Use unrounded accuracy differences (`baseline - reduced`). Negative differences are possible."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1b687b8e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "removal_candidates = [\n",
    "    \"lead_source\", \"number_of_courses_viewed\", \"interaction_count\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "removal_results = []\n",
    "for excluded in removal_candidates:\n",
    "    remaining = X_train.columns.drop(excluded).tolist()\n",
    "    reduced_accuracy, _, _ = fit_and_score(\n",
    "        X_train[remaining], X_val[remaining]\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    removal_results.append({\n",
    "        \"feature_removed\": excluded,\n",
    "        \"accuracy_without\": reduced_accuracy,\n",
    "        \"baseline_minus_reduced\": base_accuracy - reduced_accuracy,\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "elimination = pd.DataFrame(removal_results).sort_values(\"baseline_minus_reduced\")\n",
    "display(elimination)\n",
    "q5 = elimination.iloc[0][\"feature_removed\"]\n",
    "print(\"Q5 answer:\", q5)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4d2101ef",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q6 — Regularization\n",
    "\n",
    "Check the specified `C` values. Compare accuracies rounded to three decimals, and pick the **smallest C** in a tie."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1321fba",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "c_values = [0.000001, 0.00001, 0.0001, 0.001]\n",
    "regularization_results = []\n",
    "for c_value in c_values:\n",
    "    accuracy, _, _ = fit_and_score(X_train, X_val, C=c_value)\n",
    "    regularization_results.append({\n",
    "        \"C\": c_value,\n",
    "        \"accuracy\": accuracy,\n",
    "        \"accuracy_rounded_3dp\": round(accuracy, 3),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "regularization = pd.DataFrame(regularization_results)\n",
    "display(regularization)\n",
    "best_rounded = regularization[\"accuracy_rounded_3dp\"].max()\n",
    "q6 = regularization.loc[\n",
    "    regularization[\"accuracy_rounded_3dp\"] == best_rounded, \"C\"\n",
    "].min()\n",
    "print(f\"Q6 answer: {q6:g}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "87bca924",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Submission summary\n",
    "\n",
    "All six results are collected here for the [homework submission page](https://courses.datatalks.club/ml-zoomcamp-2026/homework/hw03)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "701aff92",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "answers = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    {\"Question\": \"Q1\", \"Answer\": q1},\n",
    "    {\"Question\": \"Q2\", \"Answer\": q2},\n",
    "    {\"Question\": \"Q3\", \"Answer\": q3},\n",
    "    {\"Question\": \"Q4\", \"Answer\": f\"{q4:.2f}\"},\n",
    "    {\"Question\": \"Q5\", \"Answer\": q5},\n",
    "    {\"Question\": \"Q6\", \"Answer\": f\"{q6:g}\"},\n",
    "])\n",
    "display(answers)"
   ]
  }
